{
  "requirement": "The coverage workflow returns a failing exit status when test execution or\ncoverage collection fails and reports the failure.\nCollecting coverage does not turn a failing test run into a successful command.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations derived from `requirements.test-coverage.failures`**\n1. A failure of test execution makes the coverage command exit with a failing status and reports the failure.\n2. A failure of coverage collection does the same.\n3. Collecting coverage does not turn a failing test run into a successful command.\n\n**Test execution failure (obligations 1 and 3)**\n- `tests/execution_coverage.rs#fn[real_parallel_processes_retries_child_profiles_and_filtered_reruns]` runs the `retries` test with `--retries 0`. That test fails on its first attempt.\n- The test asserts `!failed.status.success()`.\n- It asserts the saved run and attempt outcomes are `failed`, and that the failed profiles are retained.\n- In the same test, an empty selection exits with code 4, and the run records an \"Empty test selection\" diagnostic.\n- A failing test run is therefore not turned into success.\n- The failure is reported through the run and attempt metadata. It is not asserted on stderr in that test.\n- `a_process_that_cannot_start_is_failed_with_retained_attempt_metadata` covers a test process that cannot start. It asserts a failing status, a `failed` attempt outcome and the diagnostic \"Cannot start test process\".\n- `interrupting_the_parent_preserves_started_attempt_metadata` asserts exit code 130 and an `interrupted` outcome.\n\n**Coverage collection failure (obligations 2 and 3)**\n- `passing_tests_with_missing_or_corrupt_profiles_fail_collection_and_retain_partial_reports`:\n  - All tests pass, but profiles are missing or corrupt.\n  - It asserts a failing exit status and stderr containing \"partial profiles and reports have been retained\".\n  - It asserts the run outcome is `failed`.\n  - It asserts per-attempt diagnostics, and that the combined full flow fails before the \"Coverage check\" step.\n  - Collection failure is thus shown to fail the command even when the tests pass.\n- `cleanup_failure_is_reported_and_next_collection_removes_orphans` asserts a failing status and \"Permission denied\" on stderr.\n- `unreadable_build_inputs_fail_preparation_before_any_tests_start` asserts a failing status and \"Coverage preparation failed\".\n- `a_build_that_cannot_start_preserves_the_current_set` asserts a failing status.\n- `a_failed_replacement_commit_reports_the_error_without_launching_execution` asserts a failing status and the synthetic commit error on stderr.\n- `execution_startup_failure_leaves_prior_selected_results_pending_without_measurements` asserts a failing status, a `failed` run outcome and a diagnostic.\n- The compile-error case at the end of the real-process test asserts a failing status.\n\n**Unit level**\n- `src/execution_coverage/runner.rs#mod[tests]/fn[parallel_conversion_is_bounded_and_retains_every_result_in_order]` checks that a failed profile conversion is still retained in order and counted as completed.\n\n**Assessment**\nThe tests cover each failure class the requirement names, test execution and collection, at the command level. They assert a failing exit status, and most also assert a reported message or diagnostic. I found no unrepresented input class or weak assertion.",
  "references": "9bdf2ec8aecaed19a27baf6e8ceb29108016e4e095fa5dd9736b179bf57ea4f8",
